1
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:28,500
Evolution Becomes Revolution.

2
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Rise of the Planet of the Apes is a thriller, action,
drama film directed by Rupert Wyatt.

3
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:13,500
A highly intelligent chimpanzee named Caesar has been living a
peaceful suburban life ever since he was born.

4
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
But when he gets taken to a cruel primate facility, Caesar
decides to revolt against those who have harmed him.

5
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:58,500
Caesar, played by Andy Serkis.

6
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Will Rodman, played by James Franco.

7
00:30:37,500 --> 00:30:43,500
Caroline Aranha, played by Freida Pinto.

8
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Charles Rodman, played by John Lithgow.

9
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:28,500
John Landon, played by Brian Cox.

10
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Dodge Landon, played by Tom Felton.

11
00:48:07,500 --> 00:48:13,500
Rise of the Planet of the Apes is a 2011 American science fiction action film
directed by Rupert Wyatt from a screenplay by Rick Jaffa and Amanda Silver.

12
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
It is a reboot of the Planet of the Apes film series, the seventh
installment overall and the first in the reboot series.

13
00:56:52,500 --> 00:56:58,500
The film stars James Franco, Freida Pinto, John Lithgow,
Brian Cox, Tom Felton, and Andy Serkis.

14
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:21,000
Set in 2016, the film follows Caesar (Serkis), a genetically enhanced chimpanzee who is first raised by
chemist Will Rodman (Franco) before ultimately leading an ape uprising against humanity.

15
01:05:37,500 --> 01:05:43,500
Rise of the Planet of the Apes first entered development in 2006 when Jaffa and Silver wrote a spec script
and sold it to 20th Century Fox, the producers and distributors of the original film series.

16
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Production struggled until Franco, Serkis, and Wyatt were hired by late 2009, and principal photography started in July
2010 and finished that September, with filming locations including Vancouver, San Francisco, and Oahu.

17
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
The apes were created using extensive visual effects and
motion capture commissioned by Weta Digital.

18
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
Rise of the Planet of the Apes was released in the
United States on August 5, 2011.

19
01:23:07,500 --> 01:23:13,500
The film received positive reviews from critics and was a commercial success,
grossing over $481 million worldwide against a budget of $93 million.

20
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
It received numerous awards and nominations, including nominations for Best Visual Effects and Best Special
Visual Effects at the 84th Academy Awards and 65th British Academy Film Awards, respectively.

21
01:31:52,500 --> 01:31:58,500
It helped relaunch the franchise, and was followed by the sequels Dawn of the Planet of the Apes
(2014), War of the Planet of the Apes (2017), and Kingdom of the Planet of the Apes (2024).

22
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
The film explores themes of san francisco, california,
solidarity, gorilla, intelligence, dystopia.

23
01:40:37,500 --> 01:40:43,500
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
